++ 34. A `..` IN A QUALIFIED NAME REMOVES THE COMPONENT BEFORE IT, AFTER A
++     DOUBLED SLASH AND AFTER A COMPONENT STARTING WITH `.` TOO (Phase 9b
++     Task 5). OWNER: none.
++
++     Every name the oracle qualifies (`QUALIFY`, `.File`, streams, the
++     RexxUtil path arguments, `SysFileTree`'s directory part) passes through
++     `SysFileSystem::normalizePathName`
++     (interpreter/platform/unix/SysFileSystem.cpp:687-776, the same in this
++     checkout's interpreter/). It copies byte by byte into an output buffer
++     and remembers `previousSlash`, the output position a `..` returns to. It
++     sets `previousSlash` at an input `/` only when the next input byte is
++     not `.` (line 706), and before it drops a repeated `/`. So the second of
++     two slashes records the last byte of the component before them, and a
++     `..` right after a doubled slash returns there and removes nothing.
++     A component starting with `.` (`.hidden`, `..x`, `...`) never records
++     its slash, so a later `..` removes it and its parent. Measured through
++     `say qualify(n)`, oracle then this crate, probe `q.rex` in
++     docs/superpowers/records/2026-10-13-phase-9b/task-5/probes/:
++
++       `/a/b//../c`          /a/b/c   /a/c
++       `/a/b///../c`         /a/b/c   /a/c
++       `/a/b/.//../c`        /a/b/c   /a/c
++       `/a/b//..`            /a/b     /a
++       `/a/b/c/..//../d`     /a/b/d   /a/d
++       `/a/b/c//../../d`     /a/b/d   /a/d
++       `/a/.hidden/../c`     /c       /a/c
++       `/a/.config/../x`     /x       /a/x
++       `/a/b/..x/../c`       /a/c     /a/b/c
++       `/a/b/.../../c`       /a/c     /a/b/c
++
++     The oracle's answers name a different file than the one the name
++     spells. This crate removes one component per `..`, whatever precedes
++     it. Controller ruling 2026-10-13 (ledger
++     .superpowers/sdd/2026-10-13-phase-9b/progress.md), on Moritz's
++     "oracle bug" stance. The rows both sides reduce alike are witnessed in
